From 6bfa6b3b9e84c91bc547447640ebcf5f7a72a589 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:52:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH net-next 2/2] net: axienet: advertise NETIF_F_HIGHDMA

Without NETIF_F_HIGHDMA, the core copies every skb that has a fragment
in a highmem page into a linear buffer before handing it to the driver.
On a 32-bit system with HIGHMEM, such as MicroBlaze with more RAM than
CONFIG_LOWMEM_SIZE, this hits most TCP sendfile() and splice() traffic,
since page cache pages are usually in highmem.

Both TX paths can now map highmem pages: the legacy path with
skb_frag_dma_map() since the previous patch, the dmaengine path with
skb_to_sgvec() and dma_map_sg().  Set the flag.

This depends on the previous patch.  Without it, the first highmem
fragment reaches dma_map_single() with a NULL address.  On QEMU
petalogix-ml605 with 128 MB of 256 MB as highmem, sending an 8 MiB
tmpfs file with sendfile() over TCP oopses in axienet_start_xmit()
after "DMA-API: ... device driver maps memory from invalid area
[addr=00000000] [len=1460]".  With both patches the same transfer
sends over 7000 highmem fragments and arrives intact.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
index cc2110eb5af8..a2f4bd2d5630 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/xilinx/xilinx_axienet_main.c
@@ -2888,7 +2888,7 @@ static int axienet_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, ndev);
 
 	SET_NETDEV_DEV(ndev, &pdev->dev);
-	ndev->features = NETIF_F_SG;
+	ndev->features = NETIF_F_SG | NETIF_F_HIGHDMA;
 
 	/* MTU range: 64 - 9000 */
 	ndev->min_mtu = 64;
